From 00ff43671b4dfb9892ef7716267c9b38f616b4a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:06:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Bound intake owner diagnostics without discarding
 history

Why: closed-history inventories are unbounded, but a single page is capped at 6000 bytes. Sixty ordinary candidate notes made one durable occurrence permanently unplannable. Keep small inventories inline; store oversized full JSON by SHA256 in an additive journal table and publish count plus digest, atomically with the immutable page. Owner proof and delivery readback are unchanged.

Proof: regression RED on original plan_pages (60-candidate and long-singleton intake_page_oversize), GREEN 181 tests across nine intake/consumer files. Eight exact-anchor mutants killed: bound removal, boundary off-by-one, truncated details, wrong count, wrong digest, false empty inventory, early commit, non-idempotent insertion. Restart, ambiguous response readback, rollback and changing/repeated inventories covered. scripts/check: 20 checks pass. No production flakes or cadence/threshold changes.
